      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. But I'm also struggling with the concept of \"noise\" in my data. When I see high variance or results that seem inconsistent, my advisor mentions \"random error\" or \"stochastic noise\" interfering with the signal. How do I distinguish between actual meaningful variations in my subjects and just that random noise in my formal writing?",
